       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "24075808"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Component of the deuterosome, a structure that promotes de novo centriole amplification in multiciliated cells that can generate more than 100 centrioles. Deuterosome-mediated centriole amplification occurs in terminally differentiated multiciliated cells (G1/0) and not in S phase. Essential for centriole amplification and is required for CEP152 localization to the deuterosome"
    }
   ],
